+### Simultaneous overlapping notes
+
+This check checks that no simultaneous notes except `drag` have the same position in space.
+Becasue of floating point error, very close positions are also regarded as the same position.
+
+There is a boolean parameter of check.
+When it is true, only overlapping notes with truly invisible note bodies are regarded as violations.
+This includes:
+
+- Two simultaneous `hold` events with the same position.
+- Two simultaneous `flick` events with the same position and the same
+  (with small tolerance for floating point error) angle.
+- Two simultaneous `tap` events with the same position while
+  there is also another `tap` event that is simultaneous with them but does not necessarily have the same position.
+- A `hold` event and a `tap` event that are simultaneous and have the same position,
+  where the `tap` event is drawn behind the `hold` event.
+- A `flick` event and a `tap` event that are simultaneous and have the same position,
+  where the `tap` event is drawn behind the `flick` event.
+
